{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-substrate-parameter-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:substrate-parameter-exists","kind":"theorem","title":"Existence of the substrate parameter","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-substrate-parameter-exists"],"tags":["existence","substrate","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.ofReebDecomposition","text":"substrate-parameter-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:substrate-parameter-exists\"></a><p>For any quantum observable universe, the parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\mathrm{End}(\\mathbf{1})</code> exists and is distinct from roots of unity. In the archimedean realization, it specializes to a real-valued field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q(p) \\ge 1</code> interpolating the differential.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-exists.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"3.7.7"}
